Chapter: TruetypeTruncatedGuard
  cites Encode chapter TrueType
  cites Ui chapter GlyphRasterizer
  cites Ui chapter TrueTypeFont

 Track D row 19 residue, found while guarding GlyphRasterizer and assigned back
 to this lane. ttf-u8, ttf-u16, ttf-u32 and ttf-read-tag all read with bare
 list-at, and every field of every table is read at a fixed offset from a table
 offset the FILE supplied. A file that stops early is read past its end.

 Measured before the guard: ttf-parse of a font truncated anywhere in its table
 directory or its head table kills the guest. The whole ui/ leg's guards sit
 downstream of a call that never returned.

 The bytes below are codex/test/truetype-bridge-test.codex's font, byte for
 byte, cut to a series of lengths: 0, 1, 11 (inside the offset table), 12
 (exactly the offset table), 30 (inside the first table record), 60 (three
 records in), 240 (inside the head table) and 355 (one byte short).

 Row 1 is the control and carries the arm: the whole 356-byte font must still
 parse to 96 glyphs at 9x11, or a guard that answered zero everywhere would
 pass every truncated row and mean nothing.

 Row 10 is the second control: unitsPerEm read back from the intact font must
 still be 1024, which is what says ttf-byte-at did not start answering zero for
 offsets that are in range.

